IELTS Academic Listening Part 1 for a Brazilian learner, exactly as the real-AI run on 10 Oct 2026 asked it: the notice's own words for the part, its full 10 questions, every listening format allowed, no accents and no level. Two speakers arrange something in an everyday social situation for about 4 to 5 minutes (600 words or more), played once, with form or note completion: names (spelled out letter by letter), numbers, days, times and prices, several of them right after a speaker corrects themselves. Every typed question states its word limit in the question or its context the way IELTS does ("Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER."), since each question is shown on its own; every accepted answer fits that limit and reads right in its gap: numbers as digits, and in words only when the words fit ("nine thirty" is two words, so ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER accepts "9:30" but not "nine thirty"). Speakers' accents are ones IELTS recordings use, named as varieties of English. Reasons and key points are in Brazilian Portuguese.